    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\n**note**: The issue report is generated by Claude and reviewed with limited understanding from my side.\n\nImporting two Cython-3.3.0-compiled Limited API modules into one process fails when one targets `Py_LIMITED_API` < `0x030B0000` and the other targets `0x030B0000` (3.11):\n\n```\nTypeError: Shared Cython type cython_function_or_method has the wrong size, try recompiling\n```\n\nRegression from 3.2.9 (works fine there). Any process mixing abi3 wheels with different targets is affected; first seen in numpy's CI (`test_limited_api`, which builds abi3 3.9–3.15 variants — exactly the 3.11 variants fail on Linux/macOS/Windows).\n\n### Cause\n\n3.3.0 made the `__pyx_CyFunctionObject` layout depend on the Limited API target (`CythonFunction.c`, presumably via the #7519 layout rework):\n\n```c\n#if __PYX_LIMITED_VERSION_HEX < 0x030B0000\n    // Backwards compatible way of implementing PyGen_GetCode? ...\n    PyObject *func_is_coroutine;\n#endif\n```\n\nwhile `func_vectorcall` exists only for targets ≥ 3.12 (`CYTHON_VECTORCALL`).\n\nThe shared-type registry is the dict of the module named `__PYX_ABI_MODULE_NAME` = `\"_cython_\" CYTHON_ABI`, and `CYTHON_ABI`'s `__PYX_LIMITED_ABI_SUFFIX` distinguishes vectorcall builds but nothing distinguishes the `< 0x030B0000` layout. So targets 3.9/3.10 and 3.11 share one registry entry with different `basicsize`, and `__Pyx_VerifyCachedType` rejects whichever size registers second. Observed (CPython 3.14.2, Linux, gcc):\n\n| Py_LIMITED_API target | ABI module | CyFunction basicsize |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0x030A0000 | `_cython_3_3_0limitednofinalize` | 160 |\n| 0x030B0000 | `_cython_3_3_0limitednofinalize` | **152** |\n| 0x030C0000 | `_cython_3_3_0limited_vectorcallnofinalize` | 160 (no conflict) |\n\nPossible fixes: add an ABI suffix for the `< 0x030B0000` layout split, or make the layout uniform across Limited API targets.\n\n@da-woods \n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n```bash\nprintf 'def f():\\n    return 1\\n' > mod_a.pyx\ncp mod_a.pyx mod_b.pyx\nINC=$(python3 -c \"import sysconfig; print(sysconfig.get_path('include'))\")\ncython -3 mod_a.pyx && gcc -shared -fPIC -DCYTHON_LIMITED_API=1 -DPy_LIMITED_API=0x030A0000 -I$INC mod_a.c -o mod_a.so\ncython -3 mod_b.pyx && gcc -shared -fPIC -DCYTHON_LIMITED_API=1 -DPy_LIMITED_API=0x030B0000 -I$INC mod_b.c -o mod_b.so\npython3 -c \"import mod_a, mod_b\"\n```\n\nOutput with 3.3.0:\n\n```\nTypeError: Shared Cython type cython_function_or_method has the wrong size, try recompiling\n```\n\nWith 3.2.9 both import fine (basicsize 152 for both targets).\n\n\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nLimited API modules built with the same Cython version but different `Py_LIMITED_API` targets can be imported into the same process (as in ≤ 3.2.9), or are segregated into different shared ABI modules like the vectorcall builds already are.\n\n\n### OS\n\nLinux\n\n### Python version\n\n3.12\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.3\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_",
